# Python Test Environment

This repo uses `uv` for Python package management. Always activate the `.venv` virtual environment before running any Python tooling or tests.

If a test run fails due to a missing module, install it into the active env (prefer installing from the project config when possible).

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
source .venv/bin/activate
cd apps/api
uv pip install -e .
pytest
```

```bash
# ❌ BAD (no venv activated)
cd apps/api
pytest
```

## Setup

If the venv doesn't exist yet, create it with:

```bash
uv venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install -e "apps/api[dev]"
```

Or simply run `./scripts/bootstrap` which handles this automatically.
